2026-09-27|Reverse Strings Inside Matching Parentheses

Question
- Given a string `s` containing lowercase letters and parentheses, reverse the string inside every matching pair of parentheses, starting from the innermost pair, and return the final string without parentheses.

Approach
1. Maintain a stack of strings.
- The stack represents the text belonging to currently open parentheses.

2. Start with an empty string on the stack for the outside text.

3. When we see `'('`:
- Start a new empty string by pushing it onto the stack.

4. When we see a lowercase letter:
- Append it to the string at the top of the stack.

5. When we see `')'`:
- The top string represents the contents of the innermost parentheses.
- Reverse it.
- Remove that string from the stack.
- Append the reversed string to the new top of the stack.

6. At the end, the bottom stack element contains the complete answer.

Solution

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    string reverseParentheses(string s) {
        stack<string> st;
        st.push("");

        for (char ch : s) {
            if (ch == '(') {
                st.push("");
            }
            else if (ch == ')') {
                string cur = st.top();
                st.pop();

                reverse(cur.begin(), cur.end());

                st.top() += cur;
            }
            else {
                st.top() += ch;
            }
        }

        return st.top();
    }
};
```

- Example:
  `s = "(u(love)i)"`

- Inner pair `(love)` becomes `evol`.
- The outer pair now contains `u evol i`, which becomes `iloveu`.
- Final answer:
  `iloveu`

- Time Complexity: O(n²) in the worst case because reversing and concatenating nested strings can repeatedly process the same characters.
- Space Complexity: O(n), for the stack and stored characters.
